{#-
  Copyright (c) 2026 MeedyaSuite
  Licensed under the MIT License. See LICENSE file in the project root.

  cliff-subjects-only-body.tera
  ==============================

  Renders the SAME grouped "## [version] / ### Group / - subject" shape as
  cliff.toml's default [changelog].body template, but WITHOUT the
  `{% if commit.body %}...{{ commit.body }}` block that template adds.

  Why this file exists (owner decision D1, see
  .github/audits/release-notes-policy-audit-2026-07-24.md §3.2 leak L2):
  the "Full technical changelog" <details> section embedded in GitHub
  Release bodies (.github/workflows/release.yml's `ensure-release` job)
  is rendered by invoking git-cliff over a tag range with NO --body
  override, so it falls back to cliff.toml's default body template --
  the same template used to generate CHANGELOG.md. That template
  intentionally includes full multi-line commit bodies (CHANGELOG.md is
  the durable, technical developer record and is meant to). But
  commit bodies are exactly where mechanism detail lives (acquisition
  paths, credential/token names, protocol internals — see STYLE_GUIDE.md
  "Never reveal how a feature is delivered"), and the collapsed
  <details> block still ships inside the PUBLISHED, in-app-served
  release body.

  Editing cliff.toml's shared default body template directly was
  considered and rejected: changelog.yml regenerates the ENTIRE
  CHANGELOG.md from that same default template on every push to main
  (`git-cliff --config cliff.toml --output CHANGELOG.md`, no --body
  override), so stripping `commit.body` there would silently strip
  commit bodies from the whole technical changelog going forward --
  exactly the outcome D1 rules out ("The full technical record remains
  in CHANGELOG.md (unchanged)"). This file is a SEPARATE template, used
  ONLY for the release-body "Full technical changelog" <details> render,
  wired via an explicit `--body "$(cat .github/cliff-subjects-only-body.tera)"`
  override at the git-cliff invocation that produces $INC in release.yml
  (both the stable and prerelease branches read the same $INC file, and
  the self-heal path re-runs the same code block, so one wiring point
  covers all three).

  Template variables mirror cliff.toml's [changelog].body doc comment:
  version, timestamp, commits[].{group, scope, message, breaking}.
  Deliberately does NOT reference commit.body anywhere.
-#}
{%- if version %}## [{{ version | trim_start_matches(pat="v") }}] - {{ timestamp | date(format="%Y-%m-%d") }}
{%- else %}## [Unreleased]
{%- endif %}
{% for group, commits in commits | group_by(attribute="group") %}
### {{ group | striptags | trim | upper_first }}

{% for commit in commits -%}
- {% if commit.scope %}**({{ commit.scope }})** {% endif %}{% if commit.breaking %}[**BREAKING**] {% endif %}{{ commit.message | upper_first }}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor -%}
